WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
Choose a place where you can pause safely.

2
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.620
Sit, lie down, or stand with reliable support.

3
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.560
Your eyes may stay open.

4
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:21.015
This practice will not predict what happens next or ask you to feel certain.

5
00:00:22.715 --> 00:00:30.000
Its purpose is smaller: to stay near what is known in this moment while an unfinished question remains unfinished.

6
00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:36.121
Begin by noticing the room.

7
00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:46.116
Find the nearest wall or edge, the direction of the door, and one source of light.

8
00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:56.886
Let the eyes move slowly enough to register that you are here, now, in a particular place.

9
00:01:03.068 --> 00:01:07.938
Feel the points where the body meets support.

10
00:01:09.638 --> 00:01:15.828
Notice weight, pressure, temperature, and texture.

11
00:01:17.528 --> 00:01:21.243
You do not need to relax.

12
00:01:22.943 --> 00:01:34.878
Let contact be factual: the floor is here; the chair is here; the surface is carrying this much of you.

13
00:01:41.746 --> 00:01:48.106
Uncertainty often pulls attention into a future made of many possible scenes.

14
00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:55.961
Notice if the mind is rehearsing, forecasting, or searching.

15
00:01:57.661 --> 00:02:01.451
There is no need to stop it by force.

16
00:02:03.151 --> 00:02:11.161
Silently name what is happening: planning, imagining, checking, waiting.

17
00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:26.757
Now identify three facts that are true in the present and do not require interpretation.

18
00:02:28.457 --> 00:02:31.837
Perhaps: I am sitting.

19
00:02:33.537 --> 00:02:35.297
I can hear a sound.

20
00:02:36.997 --> 00:02:38.237
My hands are touching.

21
00:02:39.937 --> 00:02:41.657
Choose your own plain facts.

22
00:02:50.243 --> 00:02:56.088
Let one natural breath pass while you stay with the first fact.

23
00:02:57.788 --> 00:02:59.708
Another breath with the second.

24
00:03:01.408 --> 00:03:03.128
Another with the third.

25
00:03:04.828 --> 00:03:15.248
The breath is only a measure of time; it does not have to become slow or deep.

26
00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:32.534
Bring the unfinished question to mind only as words, not as a full scene.

27
00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.154
Keep it at a workable distance.

28
00:03:37.854 --> 00:03:41.734
You might say: I do not know yet.

29
00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:49.199
Notice what happens in the body when those words are present.

30
00:03:57.784 --> 00:04:15.179
If the response feels too strong, open your attention immediately to the room, look toward the door or window, and press gently into the surface beneath you.

31
00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:22.194
You decide how much contact to have with the question.

32
00:04:29.063 --> 00:04:34.508
If it remains workable, locate one edge of the uncertainty in the body.

33
00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:43.818
Perhaps a moving stomach, a tight throat, energy in the arms, or pressure behind the eyes.

34
00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:50.733
Then locate one neutral or steady place.

35
00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:56.643
Move between them without needing either one to change.

36
00:05:06.946 --> 00:05:17.856
Uncertainty is not the same as danger, though the body may react as if an answer is urgently needed.

37
00:05:19.556 --> 00:05:21.396
Check the present environment.

38
00:05:23.096 --> 00:05:28.031
Is there an action required right now for safety or care?

39
00:05:29.731 --> 00:05:34.556
If yes, the practice can end and you can take it.

40
00:05:36.256 --> 00:05:41.641
If no, allow this minute to be a minute of waiting.

41
00:05:51.944 --> 00:05:57.624
Notice the difference between what can be done and what cannot be completed yet.

42
00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:00.884
A message can be drafted.

43
00:06:02.584 --> 00:06:06.224
A question can be written down.

44
00:06:07.924 --> 00:06:10.044
Information can be gathered later.

45
00:06:11.744 --> 00:06:19.429
Another person’s decision, tomorrow’s result, or the whole future may not be available now.

46
00:06:29.731 --> 00:06:38.106
Imagine placing the unavailable part on a nearby shelf, not throwing it away.

47
00:06:39.806 --> 00:06:44.686
It remains important and can be picked up again.

48
00:06:46.386 --> 00:06:51.156
For these few breaths, let your hands be empty.

49
00:06:59.742 --> 00:07:01.862
Feel the palms and fingers.

50
00:07:03.562 --> 00:07:08.712
Notice whether they are gripping, pressing, or preparing.

51
00:07:10.412 --> 00:07:13.912
Let them rest against a surface.

52
00:07:15.612 --> 00:07:26.327
Keep the effort that protects or supports you; release only the effort that is working on a future answer right now.

53
00:07:34.913 --> 00:07:36.833
Return to the body’s outline.

54
00:07:38.533 --> 00:07:43.348
Feel the front, back, sides, and the space around you.

55
00:07:45.048 --> 00:07:50.778
Uncertainty may be one experience inside this wider shape.

56
00:07:52.478 --> 00:07:55.968
It is not the whole of you.

57
00:08:04.554 --> 00:08:08.584
Offer yourself a sentence that is believable.

58
00:08:10.284 --> 00:08:11.884
I can know more later.

59
00:08:13.584 --> 00:08:17.059
I can take the next clear step.

60
00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:23.514
I do not have to finish this question in this breath.

61
00:08:25.214 --> 00:08:30.984
If none fits, use simply: not known yet.

62
00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:43.566
Let silence follow the sentence.

63
00:08:45.266 --> 00:08:50.616
Notice any impulse to repeat it quickly or turn it into reassurance.

64
00:08:52.316 --> 00:08:56.186
The words do not promise an outcome.

65
00:08:57.886 --> 00:09:03.761
They mark the boundary between this moment and what has not arrived.

66
00:09:14.064 --> 00:09:29.349
Consider one value you want to carry while you wait: honesty, patience, steadiness, kindness, courage, or care.

67
00:09:31.049 --> 00:09:33.289
A value is not a prediction.

68
00:09:34.989 --> 00:09:40.254
It is a way of meeting the next available action.

69
00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:53.675
Ask what the smallest value-aligned step might be.

70
00:09:55.375 --> 00:09:59.225
It may be doing nothing for now.

71
00:10:00.925 --> 00:10:15.840
It may be writing one note, asking one clear question, resting, eating, or returning to the task in front of you.

72
00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.425
Keep the step small enough to be real.

73
00:10:30.011 --> 00:10:32.051
Come back to three present facts.

74
00:10:33.751 --> 00:10:34.831
A sound.

75
00:10:36.531 --> 00:10:38.291
A point of contact.

76
00:10:39.991 --> 00:10:43.191
A color or shape.

77
00:10:44.891 --> 00:10:50.961
Notice whether they are the same facts as before or different ones.

78
00:10:52.661 --> 00:10:58.641
The present is allowed to keep changing without providing the final answer.

79
00:11:07.226 --> 00:11:09.466
Take three ordinary breaths.

80
00:11:11.166 --> 00:11:15.761
With each exhale, feel the support beneath you.

81
00:11:17.461 --> 00:11:21.621
With each inhale, notice the room around you.

82
00:11:23.321 --> 00:11:25.521
No special rhythm is required.

83
00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:36.705
Begin to move the head, hands, and feet.

84
00:11:38.405 --> 00:11:42.415
Look toward where you will go next.

85
00:11:44.115 --> 00:11:51.340
Let the unfinished question remain on its shelf until you deliberately choose to return to it.

86
00:11:53.740 --> 00:12:00.000
Continue with the next clear thing, not the entire unknown future.
